infra/ — build infrastructure patches
======================================

These patches are applied to PDFium on every build, before any feature
patches in patches/. They are *not* counted in PATCHES_VERSION because
they don't add any FPDFRejeb_* features — they only fix the build
output to match what downstream consumers expect:

  * 0001-shared-library.patch — make `pdfium` a shared_library target
    so ninja produces libpdfium.{dylib|so|dll} instead of a static .a.
  * 0002-public-headers.patch — flatten public/cpp include paths and
    always-define FPDF_EXPORT so consumers can link without needing
    COMPONENT_BUILD.
  * 0003-android-build.patch — strip `hide_all_but_jni_onload` from
    android shared_library defaults so PDFium's exported FPDF_*
    symbols survive the link (chromium's default is to hide every
    symbol that isn't JNI_OnLoad). Lives in //build (a separate
    gclient checkout); carries an `Apply-from: build` header so
    02-apply-patches.sh routes it to the right tree.
  * 0004-ios-pdfium.patch — extend core/fxge/BUILD.gn's apple_impl
    branch from `is_mac` to `is_mac || is_ios` (PDFium gates it on
    is_mac only because Chrome doesn't ship PDFium on iOS), and drop
    the `ios_automatically_manage_certs` branch in testing/test.gni
    that references a gn arg we don't define.

All patches are vendored verbatim (with minor trim of unused Windows
metadata in 0001) from bblanchon/pdfium-binaries, BSD-3-Clause licensed.
Re-vendor when bumping PDFIUM_VERSION if upstream PDFium / //build
drifts in the patched files (BUILD.gn, public/fpdfview.h,
public/cpp/fpdf_*.h, build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn, core/fxge/BUILD.gn,
testing/test.gni).

Source: https://github.com/bblanchon/pdfium-binaries/tree/master/patches
